{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "Start",
      "text": "Welcome to the Harbor Museum. Your headset can branch between galleries whenever you choose.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "OrientationHub",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "FossilIntro",
      "text": "The fossil hall starts with a suspended mammoth and a floor map of vanished coastlines.",
      "speaker": "Curator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FossilChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "DinoNarration",
      "text": "Notice the healed fracture on the mammoth rib. It tells us the herd survived one brutal winter before the final thaw.",
      "speaker": "Curator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FossilDeepChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "ClimatePanel",
      "text": "Pollen trapped under the tusks matches a colder grassland than this city has seen in ten thousand years.",
      "speaker": "Curator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FieldStory",
      "text": "The excavation crew nicknamed this skeleton Lantern because the ice around it glowed blue at sunrise.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "AmberNarration",
      "text": "This amber drawer preserves insects, fern spores, and even one tiny feather barb caught mid-drift.",
      "speaker": "Curator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "AmberChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "InsectZoom",
      "text": "The dragonfly's wing veins still align with species that now live only in tropical wetlands.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "TradeRoute",
      "text": "Traders carried Baltic amber through ports that later fed the same shipping lanes highlighted in the maritime wing.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "TimelineBridge",
      "text": "The timeline wall links extinctions, migrations, and human toolmaking so visitors can jump between eras instead of walking chronologically.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "MaritimeIntro",
      "text": "The maritime wing mixes harbor storm recordings, navigation charts, and cargo recovered from a wreck near the old breakwater.",
      "speaker": "Narrator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "MaritimeChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "StormDeck",
      "text": "The speakers above you replay a gale recorded by lighthouse staff during the winter blackout of 1926.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "StormChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "SurvivalNote",
      "text": "Sailors tied themselves to the rail and counted bell strikes to measure distance when the stars vanished behind ice.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "WhaleBridge",
      "text": "The migration overlay shows why the museum placed the whale gallery beside maritime history instead of natural science.",
      "speaker": "Narrator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "TradeMap",
      "text": "This map layers tea, amber, and copper routes so you can trace how one harbor connected exhibitions on opposite sides of the museum.",
      "speaker": "Archivist",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "CaptainLog",
      "text": "The captain's handwriting sharpens whenever the crew sailed close to reefs, as if caution tightened every line of ink.",
      "speaker": "Archivist",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "CaptainChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "MutinyRumor",
      "text": "One margin note claims the crew hid fresh water from the paying passengers, but no court ever proved it.",
      "speaker": "Archivist",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "SailRepair",
      "text": "The patched sail overhead was stitched with modern linen so visitors can still read the original wind tears.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "LabIntro",
      "text": "The restoration lab lets you follow pigment scans, frame repairs, and conservation interviews through the glass wall.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "LabChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "PigmentScan",
      "text": "Infrared images uncovered a hidden lighthouse sketch beneath the seascape now hanging beside the lab.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "PigmentChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "UVOverlay",
      "text": "Under ultraviolet light, later varnish glows green while the original brushwork stays matte and calm.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "MineralOrigin",
      "text": "The pigment minerals came through the same shipping network highlighted in the maritime trade map.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FrameRepair",
      "text": "The oak frame is clamped in three places so the warped corner can relax before the adhesive cures.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FrameChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "DemoBench",
      "text": "A camera over the bench magnifies each brush stroke so even distant visitors can watch the filler settle into the cracks.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "EthicsNote",
      "text": "We restore enough for stability and reading, but we do not repaint history into something neater than it ever was.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "ConservatorIntro",
      "text": "Ask quickly; the solvent chamber restarts in three minutes and I need both hands free before then.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "ConservatorChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "CareersAnswer",
      "text": "Most conservators study chemistry, art history, and patient documentation long before they ever touch a public masterpiece.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "BarrierAnswer",
      "text": "Rope barriers hold back vibration as much as people, which matters when a cracked panel reacts to every footstep.",
      "speaker": "Conservator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "AccessibilityIntro",
      "text": "The accessibility desk can route you toward quieter spaces, family prompts, or a full transcript for every stop.",
      "speaker": "Access Host",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "AccessibilityChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "QuietRoute",
      "text": "The quiet route skips the storm speakers and sends you through the sculpture court before the busiest galleries fill up.",
      "speaker": "Access Host",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "QuietChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "SculptureCourt",
      "text": "The sculpture court is hushed except for filtered air and the soft hum of the skylight motors overhead.",
      "speaker": "Narrator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "SculptureChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "BronzeFocus",
      "text": "The bronze surface records fingerprints from the artist's own thumbs, left visible on purpose beside the polished ridge.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "TactileReplica",
      "text": "The replica station pairs touch-safe casts with short verbal cues so every form can be explored at your own pace.",
      "speaker": "Access Host",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "MaritimeBypass",
      "text": "The bypass summary covers the shipwreck chart and captain's log without playing the storm recording.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FamilyRoute",
      "text": "The family prompts turn each gallery into a short hunt for shapes, sounds, and clues hidden in the labels.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FamilyChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "ShellChallenge",
      "text": "Count how many shell spirals turn clockwise before you leave the maritime cabinets.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "FootprintHunt",
      "text": "The footprint trail begins in the fossil hall and loops past the mammoth map markers on the floor.",
      "speaker": "Guide",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "TranscriptSupport",
      "text": "I can send a QR transcript and explain the icon system printed on each route card.",
      "speaker": "Access Host",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "SupportChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "TranscriptSent",
      "text": "The transcript link is live for the next twenty-four hours and includes captions for every ambient audio segment.",
      "speaker": "Access Host",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "IconGuide",
      "text": "Blue icons mark optional detours, green icons mark family prompts, and silver icons mark quiet alternatives.",
      "speaker": "Access Host",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "CrossWingChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "LoopGallery",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    },
    {
      "id": "EchoReturn",
      "text": "The guide pauses so you can choose a new direction without losing your place in the tour.",
      "speaker": "Narrator",
      "type": "line"
    },
    {
      "id": "ReplayChoice",
      "text": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "type": "choice"
    }
  ],
